# `#[head]`

<SymbolMeta />
<SymbolSignature />

HEAD shorthand for `#[route(HEAD, path, ...)]` inside an HTTP `#[handlers]` implementation.

```rust
#[head("/{id}")]
async fn exists(&self, Path(id): Path<u64>) -> StatusCode { todo!() }
```

It accepts an optional controller-relative string path followed by the shared route modifiers. `#[head]` and `#[head(streamed)]` mount at the controller base. It is a consumed marker, not a standalone function attribute. See [`#[route]`](./route) for complete grammar, modifier rules, containment, generated artifacts, and feature behavior.
